{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773081336,"nonce":"Xf9kbFPvSXwqVO43DKgPuQwvsIY=","title":"beforeunload/sendBeacon: closing tab within 800ms debounce loses unsaved changes","message":"If the user closes the browser tab within 800ms of their last edit, the debounce timer has not fired and changes are lost silently.\n\nFix: add a beforeunload event listener in App.tsx that calls navigator.sendBeacon to POST the current graph state to a /api/graphs/{id}/beacon endpoint when isDirty is true.\n\nsendBeacon sends fire-and-forget, survives page unload, and does not block tab close.\nThe FastAPI endpoint must accept application/octet-stream or application/json body.","files":null}]}